        {
          "id": 2526737020,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "It only seems to gating vendor namespace handling for when we are not in TLV mode. I assume this is a leftover from when vendor namespaces where completely separate. Now there can be specific vendor TLVs which have the same index as `IEEE80211_RADIOTAP_VENDOR_NAMESPACE`. You can see handling for both cases within this statement at [packet-ieee80211-radiotap.c#L3743](https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/blob/master/epan/dissectors/packet-ieee80211-radiotap.c?ref_type=heads#L3743) but this can never be reached due to this unnecessary check.\n\nIf the `tree` condition should also be removed I am happy to do that as part of this PR.",
          "author": {
            "id": 28009592,
            "username": "a.baumann.morse",
            "public_email": null,
